The TestFile system is not correct. Should be this layout:

Test2::Harness::Role::TestFile - Defines things the Test2::Harness2 namespace needs to know about a test file
Test2::Harness::TestFile - Implementation of the role with static data, IE all required methods and fields have set values that will not change. No methods for mutating or for finding new information about the test file. If Test2::Harness2 is constructing or reconstructing a test file we should have the data already.
App::Yath2::TestFile - Implementation of the role that knows how to read important info and headers from the file.

App::Yath2 and yath commands should construct the TestFile objects using the
TestFile in App::Yath2, it should then serialize the final data built from
scanning/reading the file into a hashref, these testfile hashes are used when
queueing a run, not simply the paths to the files. The harness and run services
should get the test data already fully formed.

This will allow yath plugins (future work) and similar to modify, inject, or
construct TestFiles on the UX end. It also reduces the surface area for
exceptions, better to catch exceptions due to TestFile problems early in the
`yath test` command, as opposed to inside the harness.

In the App::Yath UX layer is also where the CLI settings can be applied to the
TestFiles.

The role can keep the defaults, TO_JSON and Rehydrate, and anything that helps
look into the data like checking if a specific featue is enabled, rank, most of
check_*, etc.

